From 700ea71b369c6da460df45d074d2a9227a857ad8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guideboard Labs <contact@guideboardlabs.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:03:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] model: add sensenova_loop

A Qwen3.5 hybrid trunk whose middle block is executed twice, with two
residual streams and a router on every sublayer of the repeated range.

The loop is expanded into one block per visit so the existing hybrid
machinery (fresh recurrent state and KV per visit) applies unchanged, and
the second visit aliases the first visit's tensors: the file stores the
block once, the graph runs it twice.

Conversion lives in conversion/sensenova.py; mHC streams and the per block
kinds travel as two GGUF keys. Vision and MTP are dropped, text only.
